  "outcome": "ESCALATE",
  "rationale": "The invoice from active vendor Consolidated Materials Group is arithmetically clean and all non-rush lines match contracted reference prices, but PR-001 flags a HIGH overcharge: the WidgetA (rush order) line is billed at $300 vs the $250 reference (20% over, well above the 5% tolerance). PR-003 notes the same item at two prices on one invoice. The free-text rush label and zero prior invoice history for this vendor give no evidence of an authorized rush schedule or accepted premium, so auto-approve is inappropriate; outright reject is also too harsh because a rush upcharge may be legitimate if someone authorized it. Please confirm with the requestor/buyer whether a rush premium was agreed (and at what rate); if yes, approve or rebill with a separate authorized rush fee; if no, return to vendor for rebill at $250/unit on that line.",
